From d1fd5fa848edbfaff527469d7de78a396aab353b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:46:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 016/108] codegen: --dump-image and --dump-functions developer
 options

--dump-image <path>: after the entrypoint XEX is loaded, write the guest image
as mapped (image_base .. image_base+image_size, big-endian, untouched) to
<path>, plus <path>.json with image_base, image_size, entry_point,
code_start/code_end (executable-section range, = REX_CODE_BASE/SIZE) and
sections (name, address, size, flags "x" when executable).

--dump-functions <path>: after the entrypoint analysis (before returning any
validation error) write '0xADDR 0xSIZE name AUTHORITY' per function, sorted
by address; names follow CodegenWriter (rexcrt_*, xstart, sub_XXXXXXXX).
With this flag the entrypoint is analysed even when its stamp is current.

Both are no-ops when absent and do not change generated output.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

